Both HTML files lacked mobile-optimized CSS, resulting in poor usability on phones and tablets.

## Changes

**index.html**
- Added base styles with fluid typography using `clamp()` for responsive text scaling
- Implemented touch-friendly sizing: 44px minimum for buttons per WCAG 2.1 AAA
- Added responsive breakpoints: 480px, 768px, 1024px with appropriate layout adjustments
- iOS optimizations: `-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch`, `-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%`

**index (1).html**
- Enhanced existing mobile menu with touch-friendly button sizing (44-52px)
- Added 16px minimum input font size to prevent iOS auto-zoom
- Extended responsive media queries to include 480px breakpoint for small phones
- Applied iOS optimizations and tap highlight colors

## Key CSS additions

```css
/* Touch targets meet accessibility standards */
button {
    min-height: 44px;
    min-width: 44px;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(232, 228, 221, 0.2);
}

/* Prevent iOS zoom and improve scrolling */
html {
    -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
}

body {
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

/* Fluid typography scales across devices */
.hero-text h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
}
```

